<title>CHILE: Chile's VTR to invest in phone service.</title>
<headline>Chile's VTR to invest in phone service.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean telecommunications company VTR SA said it will invest $300 million in equipment to allow it to offer local telephone services through its cable television network.</p>
<p>&quot;Our target is to provide local telephone services to more than a million people in Chile by 2000 with around 370,000 telephone lines in service,&quot; said general manager Jorge Salvatierra in a statement.</p>
<p>VTR is 40 percent owned by U.S. telecommunications firm SBC Communications.</p>
